Yes, it is acceptable and optimal. The brute-force approach involves iterating through all $N$ elements once to compare them and find the maximum. This has a time complexity of $O(N)$, which is the best possible as every element must be examined at least once.
```python
def find_max_brute_force(arr):
    if not arr: return None
    max_val = arr[0]
    for x in arr:
        if x > max_val:
            max_val = x
    return max_val
```
